    "result_text": "All 272 tests pass, including the new `Cp08Tests`. The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen an owner is created without a registration date, it now defaults to today's date and is returned in the owner response as `registrationDate` in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` field (readOnly, `type: string`, `format: date`) to the `Owner` response schema. The OpenAPI generator produces an `OwnerDto.registrationDate` of type `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 After building the owner from the request, if `registrationDate` is null it's set to `LocalDate.now()`. Since `OwnerFields` (the request body) has no registration date, creation always defaults to today.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added a `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table so the value persists and is read back on GET.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps `registrationDate` automatically by name (Owner \u2194 OwnerDto), and the JDBC repository picks up the column via bean-property mapping \u2014 no changes needed there. The tests run under the `hsqldb`/`spring-data-jpa` profile.",
